File: Tropical.info, Node: visualizeHypersurface, Prev: tropicalVariety, Up: Top

visualizeHypersurface -- visualize the tropical hypersurface of the given polynomial
************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        visualizeHypersurface(polyn)
        visualizeHypersurface(Valuation=>p,polyn)
        visualizeHypersurface(Valuation=>t,polyn)
  * Inputs:
      * polyn, a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, polynomial
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * Valuation (missing documentation) => a *note number:
        (Macaulay2Doc)Number,, default value null, use p-adic coefficients with
        given p
      * Valuation (missing documentation) => a *note ring element:
        (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, default value null, use coefficients in
        R[t] with given t

Description
===========

This function wraps the Polymake visualization for a tropical hypersurface
given an input polynomial. The input should be entered as a homogeneous
polynomial. Running this method opens an image in a new browser window. The
coefficients can be interpreted as p-adic coefficients or as polynomials via
the option *note Valuation: visualizeHypersurface,. Examples are commented out
because they open a new browser window.

